# Copyable in Chat — ALWAYS

**When generating any email, letter, or communication for Dee to send: ALWAYS present the full text as a copyable code block directly in the chat response.**

## The Rule

- Do NOT just write to a file and tell Dee to go open it
- Do NOT say "it's in the folder, go copy it"
- ALWAYS paste the full email body in a code block (``` ```) right in the chat so Dee can copy it immediately
- Include TO, SUBJECT, and ATTACHMENT info above or below the code block
- The file version in SEND_TO_BUYER is the backup — the chat version is what Dee uses

## Why

- Dee works fast and needs to copy/paste directly from chat
- Opening files, navigating folders, and finding the right section wastes time
- The whole point is speed — generate it, show it, Dee copies it, done

## Format

Every email presentation should look like this:

1. Code block with full email body (copyable)
2. TO: address
3. SUBJECT: line
4. ATTACH: file name and location

## This Applies To

- Buyer emails
- Supplier emails
- Subcontractor emails
- Any communication Dee needs to send
- Follow-up emails
- Thank you emails
- Any outbound correspondence

**No exceptions. Always copyable in chat.**
